1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,000
This is EarthInspect. It connects environmental observations, lessons from past disasters,

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,500
and the evidence behind every conclusion. Here's a retrospective look at the 2018 Camp Fire in California.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
These are real NASA satellite images of the same area. On the left, November eighth, 2018.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,500
On the right, October twenty-fifth. As I move the divider, you can see a large plume on the event day

5
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:34,500
that isn't there two weeks earlier. This is a visual comparison only.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Underneath is long-term context. From 2001 to 2024, regional temperature rose 0.475 degrees Celsius per decade,

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
with a 95 percent interval from 0.144 to 0.807.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,500
That's a regional trend, separate from the event imagery, and not the cause of this fire.

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Next, planning lessons. This response, a multi-channel emergency notification system,

10
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
comes from NIST's investigation of the fire.

11
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Trace it, and each link is visible: the NIST report, what it observed, and what we still don't know.

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,500
Some conditions are our own analyst mappings, and the app labels them that way.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Now I'll add one planning assumption: the community borders wildland fuels.

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,500
It's saved as an assumption, not a fact. Under it, notification becomes a candidate lead,

15
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:39,000
and the app marks that as conditional. Evacuation planning still needs local evidence about route capacity.

16
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,500
The two can work together. Neither replaces the other.

17
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Everything is saved and exportable. What you get is a planning lead you can inspect:

18
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,500
the evidence behind it, its limits, and the assumptions it depends on.
